.policy "pydantic-practice-default-factory" revision 1
.description "Give a Pydantic field whose default must differ per instance (a timestamp, a UUID, a token) a default factory, not a default computed once by a call."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. A class body runs once, at import, so `created_at: datetime = datetime.now()` on a
// Pydantic model computes one value and every instance built without that field gets it: timestamps that are stale
// by the process's age, and for ids the same UUID on every row (primary-key collisions, records overwriting each
// other). Pydantic copies a default per instance but never re-evaluates it; `Field(default_factory=...)` calls a
// callable per instance (Pydantic docs, Fields, "Default values"). Ruff's RUF009 catches the call in a standard
// library or attrs dataclass only, and B008 catches it in a function's parameter defaults.
//   class Order(BaseModel):
//       id: UUID = uuid4()                                          reported
//       code: str = uuid4().hex                                     reported: the call inside counts
//       placed_at: datetime = Field(default=datetime.now(UTC))      reported
//       _opened: datetime = PrivateAttr(default=datetime.now())     reported: a private attribute's default too
//       seen_at: datetime = utcnow()                                reported: app.timeutil's utcnow returns a now()
//       id: UUID = Field(default_factory=uuid4)                     not reported
//       launch: datetime = datetime(2020, 1, 1)                     not reported: a fixed value
// What it reads: a field of a Pydantic model (lib/pydantic's pd_field: BaseModel, RootModel, sqlmodel.SQLModel, a
// table model or not, through the run's classes in any file), a private attribute of one (`_x: T = v`, or
// `PrivateAttr(v)` / `PrivateAttr(default=v)`, annotated or not: Pydantic copies that default per instance too, the
// same value), and a field of a `pydantic.dataclasses.dataclass` (`x: T = v`, `Field(v)`, `dataclasses.field(default=
// v)`), which RUF009 does not treat as a dataclass. The default is lib/pydantic's pd_field_default: `v` of `x: T = v`,
// the default of `Field(v)` / `Field(default=v)`, or of a `Field(v)` / `Field(default=v)` in the field's
// `Annotated[T, ...]` metadata, also through a module-level alias in any module. It is reported when the default is,
// or contains outside a lambda, a call whose result differs per call, resolved through imports (`from datetime import
// datetime as dt; dt.now()`, `import uuid; uuid.uuid4()`): datetime's now/utcnow/today and date.today,
// time.time/time_ns/monotonic/perf_counter, uuid1/4/6/7, os.urandom, the secrets and random functions, Django's
// timezone.now/localtime/localdate, pendulum's and arrow's now, shortuuid, nanoid, uuid6/uuid_utils, ulid.new, and
// bson's ObjectId() with no argument. That list of library functions is a name list because nothing in the code says
// a function returns a fresh value; everything else is resolved. A def of the run (any file, a module function or a
// class's static or class method called through its class) is followed through the run's call graph to any depth:
// `utcnow()` is reported when one of its own `return` values contains such a call or a call of another such def.
// Left alone:
//   - `default_factory=` of any form (`datetime.now`, `uuid4`, `lambda: ...`), and an uncalled function as a value;
//   - a call meant to give a fixed value: `datetime(2020, 1, 1)`, `timedelta(days=1)`, `UUID("...")`, `uuid5(...)`,
//     `Decimal("0")`, `frozenset(...)`, `Path(...)`, `os.getenv(...)`, `Field(...)`, `Enum.X`, a project helper that
//     returns no such call (or returns a function that makes one);
//   - mutable literals (`tags: list[str] = []`): Pydantic copies a mutable default for each instance, so they are
//     safe on a model (unlike a plain class or a dataclass);
//   - `ClassVar` annotations (class attributes, not fields), and unannotated `_x = datetime.now()` (Pydantic makes it a
//     private attribute too, but the unannotated form reads as a class constant and its intent is unclear);
//   - settings models (`pydantic_settings.BaseSettings` and their subclasses): a settings object is the process's
//     configuration, read once by design, and a factory would make two `Settings()` instances disagree, e.g.
//     with `SECRET_KEY: str = secrets.token_urlsafe(32)` one Settings() would sign a token with one key and another
//     check it with a different one; following the message there could break working code;
//   - non-Pydantic classes: plain classes, stdlib and attrs dataclasses (Ruff RUF009), SQLAlchemy `mapped_column(
//     default=...)` (the sqlalchemy pack), `pydantic.v1` models (pd_model leaves them out), and function parameter
//     defaults (Ruff B008);
//   - test code (lib/pydantic's pd_test_doc): a model defined in a test is a fixture of that test.
// Gaps: a field of a model whose Pydantic base is outside the run and not a known base (a library's model subclass);
// a method called on an instance (`self.clock.now()`), whose class is not resolved; a value returned through a
// variable (`t = datetime.now(); return t`); a volatile call of a library not listed; `pydantic.v1` models, which
// have the same bug.

#include "lib/pydantic.rerail"

.violation DefaultEvaluatedOnce(at: node, fn: symbol, maker: symbol) "{fn} runs once at import, so every instance shares its value. Use `{maker}(default_factory=...)` (e.g. `uuid4`, `lambda: datetime.now(timezone.utc)`) unless all instances must share it."
// A call of a listed library function is read in its own file; a def of the run it calls may be another module's,
// followed by symbol (dfo_helper); a default in a module-level alias of another module is reported in that module when
// a field of a model names the alias (dfo_alias_used).
DefaultEvaluatedOnce(k, x, m) :- dfo_site(k, m), dfo_volatile_call(k, q), x = cat("`", q, "()`").
DefaultEvaluatedOnce(k, x, m) :- dfo_site(k, m), dfo_callee(k, q), dfo_helper(q, q2),
    x = cat("`", q, "()` (it returns `", q2, "()`)").
DefaultEvaluatedOnce(k, x, "Field") :- dfo_alias_site(k, g), dfo_alias_used(g), dfo_volatile_call(k, q),
    x = cat("`", q, "()`").
DefaultEvaluatedOnce(k, x, "Field") :- dfo_alias_site(k, g), dfo_alias_used(g), dfo_callee(k, q), dfo_helper(q, q2),
    x = cat("`", q, "()` (it returns `", q2, "()`)").

// dfo_stop: code in a lambda or def runs when it is called, not when the class body runs.
.decl dfo_stop(k: symbol)
dfo_stop("lambda"). dfo_stop("function_definition").
// dfo_site(k, maker): call k is, or is in (outside a lambda or def), a default of this file (dfo_default), outside
// test code.
.decl dfo_site(k: node, maker: symbol)
dfo_site(k, m) :- dfo_default(d, m), (k = d ; within_stop(k, d, dfo_stop)), docof(k, doc), !pd_test_doc(doc).
// dfo_alias_site(k, g): call k is, or is in, the default of a Field that module-level alias g of this file holds
// (lib/pydantic's pd_global_default), outside test code.
.decl dfo_alias_site(k: node, g: symbol)
dfo_alias_site(k, g) :- pd_global_default(g, d), (k = d ; within_stop(k, d, dfo_stop)), docof(k, doc),
    !pd_test_doc(doc).

// ---- the defaults ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfo_default(d, maker): d is the default expression of a model field, a model's private attribute, or a Pydantic
// dataclass field; maker is the call the message proposes for its default_factory.
.decl dfo_default(d: node, maker: symbol)
dfo_default(d, "Field") :- pd_field(c, _, a, _), !pd_settings(c), pd_field_default(a, d).
dfo_default(d, "PrivateAttr") :- dfo_private(c, d), !pd_settings(c).
dfo_default(d, m) :- dfo_pdc_default(d, m).
// dfo_alias_use_q(g): a field of a model of this file (not a settings model) names g, a module-level alias of another
// module, in its annotation (lib/pydantic's pd_ann_global). dfo_alias_used(g): some file's model does: the alias's
// module reads it by g, on purpose across files, holding no node.
.decl dfo_alias_use_q(g: symbol)
dfo_alias_use_q(g) :- pd_field(c, _, _, t), !pd_settings(c), pd_ann_global(t, g).
.decl dfo_alias_used(g: symbol) cross_file
dfo_alias_used(g) :- dfo_alias_use_q(g).

// dfo_private(c, d): model c's private attribute gets default d: `_x: T = d`, or `PrivateAttr(d)` /
// `PrivateAttr(default=d)` assigned to `_x`, annotated or not.
.decl dfo_private(c: node, d: node)
dfo_private(c, d) :- pd_model(c), pd_class_ann(c, x, a, t), prefix("_", x), !prefix("__", x), !pd_classvar(t),
    field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, d), !dfo_privateattr_call(d).
dfo_private(c, d) :- pd_model(c), dfo_class_asg(c, x, k), prefix("_", x), !prefix("__", x), dfo_privateattr_call(k),
    dfo_default_arg(k, d).
// dfo_class_asg(c, x, k): class c's body assigns `x = k` or `x: T = k` (k unparenthesized).
.decl dfo_class_asg(c: node, x: symbol, k: node)
dfo_class_asg(c, x, k) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "body", b), body_stmt(b, s, _),
    kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, a, 0), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l),
    kind(l, "identifier"), text(l, x), field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, k).
.decl dfo_privateattr_call(k: node)
dfo_privateattr_call(k) :- kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), sym_of(f, q),
    (q = "pydantic.PrivateAttr" ; q = "pydantic.fields.PrivateAttr").
// dfo_default_arg(k, d): d is the default call k passes, positionally first or as `default=`; Ellipsis is none.
.decl dfo_default_arg(k: node, d: node)
dfo_default_arg(k, d) :- kind(k, "call"), posarg(k, 0, d), !kind(d, "ellipsis").
dfo_default_arg(k, d) :- kind(k, "call"), call_arg(k, -1, "default", d), !kind(d, "ellipsis").

// dfo_pdc(c): class c is decorated with `pydantic.dataclasses.dataclass`, bare or called.
.decl dfo_pdc(c: node)
dfo_pdc(c) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), decorator(c, e), unparen(e, m), sym_of(m, q), dfo_pdc_maker(q).
dfo_pdc(c) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), decorator(c, e), unparen(e, m), kind(m, "call"), field(m, "function", f),
    sym_of(f, q), dfo_pdc_maker(q).
.decl dfo_pdc_maker(q: symbol)
dfo_pdc_maker("pydantic.dataclasses.dataclass").
.decl dfo_dc_field_call(k: node)
dfo_dc_field_call(k) :- kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), sym_of(f, "dataclasses.field").
// dfo_pdc_default(d, maker): a Pydantic dataclass field's default: `x: T = d`, `Field(d)`, `Field(default=d)`, or
// `dataclasses.field(default=d)`.
.decl dfo_pdc_default(d: node, maker: symbol)
dfo_pdc_default(d, "Field") :- dfo_pdc(c), pd_class_ann(c, _, a, t), !pd_classvar(t), field(a, "right", v),
    unparen(v, d), !pd_field_call(d), !dfo_dc_field_call(d).
dfo_pdc_default(d, "Field") :- dfo_pdc(c), pd_class_ann(c, _, a, t), !pd_classvar(t), field(a, "right", v),
    unparen(v, k), pd_field_call(k), dfo_default_arg(k, d).
dfo_pdc_default(d, "dataclasses.field") :- dfo_pdc(c), pd_class_ann(c, _, a, t), !pd_classvar(t),
    field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, k), dfo_dc_field_call(k), call_arg(k, -1, "default", d).

// ---- calls whose result differs per call -------------------------------------------------------------------------
// dfo_callee(k, q): call k's function resolves to q.
.decl dfo_callee(k: node, q: symbol)
dfo_callee(k, q) :- kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", f), sym_of(f, q).
// dfo_volatile_call(k, q): call k of q returns a per-call value. bson's ObjectId does only with no argument.
.decl dfo_volatile_call(k: node, q: symbol)
dfo_volatile_call(k, q) :- dfo_callee(k, q), dfo_once(q).
dfo_volatile_call(k, q) :- dfo_callee(k, q), (prefix("secrets.", q) ; prefix("random.", q)), !dfo_not_volatile(q).
dfo_volatile_call(k, q) :- dfo_callee(k, q), (q = "bson.ObjectId" ; q = "bson.objectid.ObjectId"),
    !call_arg(k, _, _, _).
// The same list as the django pack's django-practice-default-called-once, plus the libraries Pydantic code uses.
.decl dfo_once(q: symbol)
dfo_once("uuid.uuid1"). dfo_once("uuid.uuid4"). dfo_once("uuid.uuid6"). dfo_once("uuid.uuid7").
dfo_once("os.urandom"). dfo_once("time.time"). dfo_once("time.time_ns"). dfo_once("time.monotonic").
dfo_once("time.monotonic_ns"). dfo_once("time.perf_counter"). dfo_once("time.perf_counter_ns").
dfo_once("datetime.datetime.now"). dfo_once("datetime.datetime.utcnow"). dfo_once("datetime.datetime.today").
dfo_once("datetime.date.today").
dfo_once("django.utils.timezone.now"). dfo_once("django.utils.timezone.localtime").
dfo_once("django.utils.timezone.localdate"). dfo_once("django.utils.crypto.get_random_string").
dfo_once("pendulum.now"). dfo_once("pendulum.today"). dfo_once("arrow.now"). dfo_once("arrow.utcnow").
dfo_once("shortuuid.uuid"). dfo_once("nanoid.generate"). dfo_once("ulid.new").
dfo_once("uuid6.uuid6"). dfo_once("uuid6.uuid7"). dfo_once("uuid_utils.uuid4"). dfo_once("uuid_utils.uuid7").
// dfo_not_volatile(q): names in secrets and random that are classes, comparisons or state, not a fresh value.
.decl dfo_not_volatile(q: symbol)
dfo_not_volatile("secrets.SystemRandom"). dfo_not_volatile("secrets.compare_digest").
dfo_not_volatile("random.Random"). dfo_not_volatile("random.SystemRandom"). dfo_not_volatile("random.seed").
dfo_not_volatile("random.getstate"). dfo_not_volatile("random.setstate"). dfo_not_volatile("random.shuffle").

// dfo_helper(q, q2): q is a def of the run with a `return` of its own whose value contains (not inside a lambda or a
// nested def) a call of q2, a per-call value, or a call of another such def of the run, to any depth:
// `def utcnow(): return datetime.now(timezone.utc)`, `def stamp(): return utcnow().isoformat()`. Each def's file says
// what its returns call, by symbol (dfo_ret_volatile_q, dfo_ret_callee_q); the chain joins the defs' modules by
// symbol, on purpose, holding no node.
.decl dfo_helper(q: symbol, q2: symbol) cross_file
dfo_helper(q, q2) :- dfo_ret_volatile_q(q, q2).
dfo_helper(q, q2) :- dfo_ret_callee_q(q, q1), q1 != q, dfo_helper(q1, q2).
.decl dfo_ret_volatile_q(q: symbol, q2: symbol)
dfo_ret_volatile_q(q, q2) :- dfo_return_call(q, k), dfo_volatile_call(k, q2).
.decl dfo_ret_callee_q(q: symbol, q1: symbol)
dfo_ret_callee_q(q, q1) :- dfo_return_call(q, k), dfo_callee(k, q1).
// dfo_return_call(q, k): call k sits in a `return` value of def q of this file.
.decl dfo_return_call(q: symbol, k: node)
dfo_return_call(q, k) :- kind(g, "function_definition"), qualname(g, q), kind(r, "return_statement"),
    nearest(r, g, fdef), within_stop(k, r, dfo_stop), kind(k, "call").

// The cases, `cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/`, read as one repository: each line ending in `# caught` is
// reported, and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "app/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/__init__.py"
    .fixture "app/base.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/base.py"
    .fixture "app/clock.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/clock.py"
    .fixture "app/dataclass_models.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/dataclass_models.py"
    .fixture "app/events.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/events.py"
    .fixture "app/jobs.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/jobs.py"
    .fixture "app/models.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/models.py"
    .fixture "app/near_misses.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/near_misses.py"
    .fixture "app/settings.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/settings.py"
    .fixture "app/timeutil.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/app/timeutil.py"
    .fixture "pyproject.toml" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/pyproject.toml"
    .fixture "tests/__init__.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "tests/test_models.py" from "../cases/pydantic-practice-default-factory/tests/test_models.py"
    .expect _ at "app/clock.py":47
    .expect _ at "app/clock.py":49
    .expect _ at "app/dataclass_models.py":12
    .expect _ at "app/dataclass_models.py":13
    .expect _ at "app/dataclass_models.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/dataclass_models.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/events.py":11
    .expect _ at "app/events.py":12
    .expect _ at "app/events.py":13
    .expect _ at "app/events.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":14
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":19
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":21
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":22
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":32
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":33
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":34
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":35
    .expect _ at "app/jobs.py":36
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":15
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":16
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":17
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":18
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":19
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":20
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":21
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":22
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":23
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":24
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":25
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":26
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":28
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":31
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":32
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":33
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":37
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":41
    .expect _ at "app/models.py":46
.end
